Subject: dplyr - error joining on yearmon dates
Message-ID: <z9REdD8Dbs4.a8RE1W76AwAJ@manipulatr.groups.google.com>
Archived-At: <https://groups.google.com/g/manipulatr/c/z9REdD8Dbs4/m/a8RE1W76AwAJ>
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

I get the following when I try and do a join on dates with the class of yearmon:

> Joining by: "dates"
> Error: cannot join on columns 'dates' x 'dates': Can't join on 'dates' x 'dates' because of incompatible types (yearmon / yearmon)

Is this expected? I wouldn't be surprised if I'm doing it wrong. However, looking at various issues and discussion leading up to #1105 <https://github.com/hadley/dplyr/issues/1105> I think this should work.

I'm using the latest lazyeval and dplyr from github.

--pete

Example:

library(dplyr)
library(zoo)

foo <- structure(list(dates = structure(c(2L, 1L, 3L),
                                        .Label = c("Feb 2015",
                                                   "Jan 2015",
                                                   "Mar 2015"),
                                        class = "factor"),
                      var1 = c(1, 2, 3)),
                 .Names = c("dates", "var1"),
                 row.names = c(NA, -3L),
                 class = "data.frame")

bar <- structure(list(dates = structure(c(2L, 1L, 3L),
                                        .Label = c("Feb 2015",
                                                   "Jan 2015",
                                                   "Mar 2015"),
                                        class = "factor"),
                      var2 = c(10, 20, 30)),
                 .Names = c("dates", "var2"),
                 row.names = c(NA, -3L),
                 class = "data.frame")

baz <- full_join(foo, bar) # ok

foo$dates <- as.yearmon(foo$dates)
bar$dates <- as.yearmon(bar$dates)

qux <- full_join(foo, bar) # nope

