MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

This should work:

bsdf <- group_by(df, ts) %>%
  do(bs = boot(.$dat, R = 10, statistic = bsmean))

bsdf %>% mutate(
  mean = bs$t0,
  var = var(bs$t)
)

but doesn't probably because the support for $ is not great yet.
Unfortunately the dplyr support for list columns is still a work in
progress. I filed an issue at
https://github.com/hadley/dplyr/issues/1400

Hadley

